              <summary><h3>What is the best protein powder at Target?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  For most people it is Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard 100% Whey in the 3.96 lb tub, at about $1.44 per 25 g of protein at Target's listed price, with a short label and a long track record. Premier Protein gives more protein per scoop for similar money, Orgain is the best plant option, and Isopure suits low-carb or lactose-sensitive shoppers.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Does Target have its own brand of protein powder?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Yes. Target's up&up brand sells a whey protein powder in chocolate and vanilla, listed at $25.99 for a 32 oz tub of about 21 servings at the time of writing. We could not find a Good & Gather protein powder; that brand sells protein bars and bites instead. The up&up label includes maltodextrin and lists no third-party certification.
                </p>
              </div>
