        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Target is a good place to buy protein powder if you shop by the gram rather than by the tub. The big Optimum Nutrition tub and Premier's 30 g powder both land under $1.50 per 25 g at listed prices, Orgain's large tub is a sound dairy-free choice, and Isopure earns its premium only for low-carb or lactose-sensitive shoppers. Target's up&up whey is cheapest of all, with a busier label to match.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Run the cost-per-25 g sum at the shelf, buy the biggest tub of a flavor you already like, and use Target Circle offers when they appear rather than waiting for them. If you compete in a tested sport, check the certifier's database first. And if you are managing a health condition, talk to a doctor or registered dietitian before adding a protein supplement.
          </p>
